WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:12.990
David Whalen: The liberal arts are those disciplines
the knowledge which of is necessary to lead

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:22.320
a completely humane life. It's probably best
to describe a liberal education as an education

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:32.320
in things worth knowing inherently, things
that a human life is rendered somewhat incomplete,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:42.760
somewhat undeveloped, somewhat unfulfilled
by not knowing. Just as health is the proper

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:49.140
good state and condition of the body, so a
disciplined, informed, robust understanding

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:53.940
of reality is the proper state or condition
of the human mind.

00:00:53.940 --> 00:01:00.120
The point is to lead rich human lives, and
humans naturally desire the good, they naturally

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:06.439
desire the true, and they naturally desire
the beautiful. We're asking what do people

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:13.510
need to know, and let's require them to know
it. About half one's time here is spent in

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:18.940
what we call the core curriculum. That will
include a study of literature, a study of

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:25.870
history, a study of the Constitution and politics.
It will include the study of biology and mathematics

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:34.210
and chemistry and physics. It will include
the study of fine arts and social sciences

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:43.600
like sociology or psychology or economics.
It's rich and full, as is your own intellectual

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:49.760
nature. Let's bring those two together. That's
a Hillsdale College liberal education.

